/*
overrideCommand
---------------

Decides whether supporting services/tools defined in `.devcontainer.json`
should replace the container’s default command with a simple
keep-alive loop:

    /bin/sh -c "while sleep 1000; do :; done"

This loop prevents the container from shutting down if its normal command
exits immediately.

• **true**  – Run the keep-alive loop instead of the image’s default command
              (default for images built from a Dockerfile).
• **false** – Run the image’s default command; choose this when the container
              must start its normal entrypoint to function.

Default behaviour:
  • `true` when using an image or Dockerfile
  • `false` when using a Docker Compose file

Test note: a file named **test** is created in the container’s root (`/`)
directory.
*/

{
  "name": "1_9-spec_overrideCommand_false",
  "build": {
    "dockerfile": "./Dockerfile"
  },
  "overrideCommand": false
}